First Author: Zadeh
Title: Predictive analytics for de novo malignancies after lung transplantation
Source number: 75

Very short summary: This retrospective US national-registry study analysed 30,917 lung transplant recipients without a documented pretransplant malignancy, of whom 25% developed a de novo malignancy during follow-up. Multiple supervised machine-learning methods were compared using a 70:30 internal split and oversampling; Gradient Boosting performed best, with a test-set AUC of 0.746, accuracy of 69.0%, sensitivity of 73.1%, and specificity of 64.9%.

